Z||000000||xythos||11-03-2000||12:47 AM||||I am planning on starting a v8 swap with Archie's kit this summer (brakes and susp. work being done now) and I would love some info from people who have bought a new crate engine to use in the conversion.  I am looking at the zz4, LT1, AND LS1 (all 350's).  So far the LS sounds like the way to go, but I dunno...<BR>I am somewhat concerned about emissions, but I am to power hungry to mess with any v6's. <BR>(I just can't see getting ANYWHERE the power from a v6.  Yes a s/c v6 is a beast, but a s/c v8 is a titan, imho)<BR>Has anyone used any of these kits? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||11-03-2000||08:37 AM||||The LS1 is an all aluminum engine I believe and that swap will be very expensive. I know several truck guys that swear by the ZZ4 crate motors. If they have enough power to make a heavy truck seem impressive, think what it will do in a Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://www.paceparts.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.paceparts.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||xythos||11-06-2000||07:14 PM||||Yea, the LS1 is alum. but that is what I like, it keeps the weight closer to the stock v6 when you have alum.  heads as well...  I will look into the LT4, because I am looking at about 7000 for a low milage LS1, can you say ouch?<BR>All I know is I gotta do something, these VTEC 4 cyl. Hondas can easily embarrass the hell out my stock fiero...<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000003||Zorba||11-06-2000||08:48 PM|||| I had a ZZ4 motor in my stretched testarossa (SOLD) and there weren't very many cars who could keep up with me or take off ahead of me at the light. You can't go wrong with a ZZ4 especially the zz430 which is rare but there are clones for about $3,000. I have also seen some 383 strokers with 450hp starting at about $2,900. Can't go wrong with those. Emissions, check your state laws for "waivers" I used "waivers" every year on my testarossa. <BR>California has no waivers I know of though because of the da*&gt;* smog law.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||11-06-2000||09:13 PM||||Waivers?  Under what basis?  Hmm I will have to see if my crappy state has them...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000005||AkursedX||11-07-2000||10:08 AM||||I don't think Archie's kit will work with an LS-1.<BR>I can remember a while back Archie posting something about how the LS-1 needed a ton of new parts fabricated to make it possible and that he was working on making a kit for it.<P>Maybe Archie has more info on this, but you might want to check to make sure.<BR>||||reg||4
